# Git and PR Rules

Read `docs/agents/git-workflow.md` before branching or opening PRs.

**All feature and UI work happens on branches — never direct commits to `main`.**

## Mandatory workflow

1. **Before any UI or feature work** — confirm an open GitHub issue exists (or ask the user to create one); verify MVP scope per `scope-mvp.mdc`
2. **Create a branch from latest `main`** — `git fetch origin && git checkout main && git pull origin main`, then `git checkout -b <type>/<issue>-<description>`
3. **Work on that branch only** — one issue, one focused change set per branch
4. **Commit and open PR only when the user explicitly asks** — do not surprise-commit or auto-open PRs

## Branch rules

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Branch format | `<type>/<issue>-<description>` (e.g. `feat/12-request-intake-form`) |
| Types | `feat/`, `fix/`, `docs/`, `test/`, `refactor/`, `chore/` — see git-workflow.md |
| Scope | One issue per branch; one focused change set per PR |
| UI redesigns | Large UI changes (including redesigns in progress) get their own branch when the user asks to commit (e.g. `feat/NN-ui-redesign`) |
| Never on main | Do not commit feature or UI work directly to `main` |

## PR size

| Size | Lines changed | Action |
|------|---------------|--------|
| Ideal | < 400 | Open PR |
| Large | 400–800 | Split if possible |
| Too large | > 800 | Must split into stacked PRs — see git-workflow.md |

PR must link to issue: `Closes #N`

## Agent checklist — before starting work

- [ ] Open GitHub issue exists and is in MVP scope (`docs/spec/mvp-scope.md`)
- [ ] Issue is NOT in `docs/spec/out-of-scope.md`
- [ ] On latest `main` (fetched and pulled)
- [ ] Feature branch created: `<type>/<issue>-<description>`
- [ ] Not editing on `main` for feature/UI changes

## Agent checklist — before commit/PR (user must ask first)

- [ ] User explicitly requested commit and/or PR
- [ ] Branch name follows convention
- [ ] Single issue scope; no unrelated refactors or out-of-scope files
- [ ] Diff under ~400 lines (or work split into stacked PRs)
- [ ] PR description has summary, `Closes #N`, and test plan
- [ ] No secrets, `.env`, or credentials in the diff

## Do not

- Commit feature work directly to `main`
- Force-push to `main` or `master`
- Auto-merge PRs
- Skip hooks (`--no-verify`) without user approval
- Commit or open PR without explicit user request
- Mix multiple issues in one branch or PR
- Refactor unrelated code "while you are here"
